# Editor / tooling
.aider*
.vscode/
.qt/

# Build trees (cmake/make) — every variant: build/ build-asan/ build-tsan/ build-gcc15/
# build_test_migration/ build_lateral_probe/ build-make-copilot/ cmake-build*/ …
# NOTE: generated/ is intentionally NOT ignored — the robocompdsl Ice stubs are committed; only the
# build output UNDER it (*_autogen/) and the in-source cmake droppings are ignored.
build*/
cmake-build*/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
*_autogen/
.trt_cache/

# Compiled / binary output
bin/
*.o
*.so
*.a
a.out
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Large ML model weights (too big for git; regenerate/export locally)
*.onnx
*.pt
*.engine

# Run artifacts + scratch edits/backups
# Per-component run logs (chair's ai2_log.csv, ring_metaconcept's ring_fit.csv, …).
# NOTE: a bare `etc/*.csv` contains a slash, so git anchors it to THIS directory and it
# never matched <component>/etc/ — `git add <component>/` then silently staged run logs.
# (.gitignore has no trailing comments: a `#` after the pattern becomes part of it.)
**/etc/*.csv
# Rotated previous runs, kept beside the live file by rc::diag::open_rotating
# (common/diag_log/rotating_csv.h): "<name>.csv.<YYYYmmdd_HHMMSS>". The rule above does NOT
# cover these — the timestamp comes AFTER the extension, so the name does not end in .csv.
**/etc/*.csv.*
# ...and the same one level down: `**/etc/*.csv` does NOT match `etc/archive/foo.csv`,
# which is how a 6.7 MB archived run log stayed tracked under a rule meant to cover it.
**/etc/**/*.csv
*.log
*.bak
*.back
*.new
*.poisoned*

# Scratch / throwaway experiments
caca/

# Large non-source blobs. GitHub HARD-REJECTS any file over 100 MB, so one of these in a
# commit blocks the whole push — retina/models.tar.gz is 1.3 GB. These are build/runtime
# assets fetched or produced locally, not repository content.
**/models.tar.gz
# Captured frame dumps (retina/etc/depth_frames held 1108 jpgs).
**/etc/depth_frames/

# ── Diagnostics written to the AGENT'S CWD, which is the COMPONENT ROOT, not etc/ ──────────────
# An agent launched as `bin/controller etc/config.toml` has its component directory as CWD, so a
# relative path like "tracker_diag.csv" lands in controller/, NOT controller/etc/. The `**/etc/*.csv`
# rules above therefore never matched them, and 39 run logs in controller/ plus 8 in room_concept/
# sat untracked in every `git status` — 130 lines of noise that a real untracked source file would
# have hidden in.
# ★ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH AND EXACTLY ONE LEVEL: `/*/` matches <component>/ and nothing
# deeper, so it cannot swallow common/**, etc/**, or anything a subdirectory legitimately tracks.
/*/*.csv
/*/*.csv.*
/*/*.jsonl

# Self-calibration output and last-known state. These are RUNTIME ESTIMATES the agents rewrite as
# they run, not configuration: committing one is committing an arbitrary instant of a continuously
# moving value, and it is dirty again the moment the robot does. Named individually rather than as
# `**/etc/*.txt`, which would also catch real config (retina/etc/tsan_suppressions.txt) and the
# world snapshots the offline benches replay (route_world.txt).
/room_concept/etc/camera_calib_*.txt
/room_concept/etc/image_edge_replay_*.txt
/room_concept/etc/last_robot_pose.txt

# In-source cmake droppings. The build* / CMakeFiles rules above miss the top-level Makefile that an
# in-source `cmake .` leaves in the component root and in generated/.
/*/Makefile
/*/generated/Makefile

# Dated/labelled backups. `*.bak` above does not match `p3bot.json.bak.pre-body` or
# `shadow.json.before.lidar.change` — the suffix continues past the extension.
*.bak.*
*.before.*
*.before-*
*.orig

# Per-run archives created by ControllerMission::archive_on_stop (a timestamped copy of each
# diagnostic beside the run). The live files are ignored above; these are their history.
**/etc/runs/
